Welcome to Deepsafer!

Here are a few simple steps to get up and running with Deepsafer Password Manager:


1. Install the browser extension
============

Autofill passwords, save new logins, access the password generator, and more from the Deepsafer browser extension. The extension keeps Deepsafer easily accessible so you can be secure while online.
Install the extension (http://www.vault.deepsafer.ye/download)


2. Add passwords to your vault
============

Your secure vault is ready to safely store your sensitive information. Add logins, credit cards, notes, and identities for fast access and autofilling!
Add passwords to your vault ({{{WebVaultUrl}}}/?utm_source=welcome_email&utm_medium=email)


3. Keep your master password safe and enable biometrics
============

Vault security starts with your Deepsafer master password. Ensure it is strong and complex, then memorize it or store it in a safe place. Now you're ready to enable biometrics for a faster login experience with fingerprint or FaceID.
Enable biometrics (https://vault.deepsafer.ye/learning/unlock-your-vault-with-biometrics/)


Learning Center
============

Instructional videos and best practice guides for every level are just a click away.
Visit the learning center (https://vault.deepsafer.ye/learning/)


Bring Deepsafer to Work
============

Are you using Deepsafer for personal or family use? Join the Deepsafer fans who are bringing the password manager they know and love to their workplace.
Bring it (https://vault.deepsafer.ye/go/bring-deepsafer-to-work/)


Signed up for Deepsafer Secrets Manager?
============

If you signed up for Deepsafer Secrets Manager to secure infrastructure and machine secrets, get up and running quickly with the Secrets Manager quick start resource (https://vault.deepsafer.ye/help/secrets-manager-quick-start/).


Stay safe and secure,
The Deepsafer Team
